k2 study zen — Zen Gardens in one page

WHAT
  Zen Mode is a mode of a K2 desktop window. In Zen the window shows a
  Garden: a personal page that lives on this computer, in
  ~/.k2/zen/gardens/<id>.toml. Agents build Gardens by editing that file
  when the human asks ("In my Zen Garden ... (id g-...)").

THE ONE RULE
  Every page keeps two buttons the human can reach in one click: the Zen
  toggle (the way out) and the Garden switcher. Where they sit, and
  whether usage, the theme control or a menu is shown, is the page's
  choice. k2 zen validate refuses a file that drops one.

THE LOOP
  k2 zen garden list                 find the Garden's id
  edit ~/.k2/zen/gardens/<id>.toml
  k2 zen validate --garden <id>      before you say it's done

THE FULL GUIDE
  k2 zen guide                       short pages; no daemon needed
  k2 zen guide gardens               start here
  k2 zen guide example --list        whole files you can pipe

USING THE WHOLE CANVAS
  On a full canvas ([layout] canvas = "full") K2's top band floats over
  a custom widget and drags the window. The widget takes clicks there
  with k2.canvas.setHitRegions(rects) (frame-viewport CSS px, [] clears,
  at most 32) and drags the window from its own element with
  k2.window.startDrag() in a mousedown. K2's controls always win, and
  some drag space always stays. Details: k2 zen guide api.

LOCKED GARDENS
  A locked Garden: don't edit it. Ask the person. k2 zen garden list
  marks it locked; K2 puts back any edit to its file, refuses k2 zen
  changes to it (exit 3, garden_locked), and only the person unlocks
  it, in Settings → Gardens.

WRITE THROUGH K2, OR PROPOSE
  k2 zen garden put <id> --from page.toml   (checked; refused if it has errors)
  k2 zen widget put <name> index.html --from index.html
  Without "Manage Gardens and data sources" a put is a PROPOSAL: nothing
  is written until a person approves it (k2 zen proposals; withdraw your
  own with reject). With it (the owner/admin turns it on per agent:
  Settings → Workspaces → <ws> → Agent) a put writes now, garden new makes
  a Garden, and you may approve proposals; each act is logged with your
  session. Never K2's built-in widgets (k2:<name>) or defaults: copy one
  with k2 zen widget new <name> --from k2:<name>.

THE WIDGET DEV LOOP (keep your widget outside ~/.k2)
  k2 zen validate --dir ./board              check; writes nothing
  k2 zen widget preview --dir ./board --config sources=fleet
                                             K2's own "Widget preview" Garden,
                                             never one of the person's
  k2 zen widget put board --dir ./board      the whole folder, one checked
                                             write (errors: nothing written;
                                             --prune drops files it lacks)
  k2 zen validate --garden <id> --from page.toml   a staged page, unwritten
  k2 zen widget errors board                 runtime errors and refusals
  validate never signs (--widget --sign does) and "pending" (not run in a
