EOF
}

cmd_help_mail_draft() {
    cat <<'EOF'
Save a DRAFT into your human's linked Gmail/IMAP Drafts folder (APPEND
\Draft). Two forms: reply onto a listed message, or compose a brand-new
To/Subject. Your human sees it in their own mail client, reviews, edits,
and sends it themselves.

`draft` only DRAFTS — it never sends. Sending FROM a linked account needs
level `send` AND workspace Sending=`on` (`k2 mail send`/`reply`;
app-password and Gmail-OAuth; Microsoft-OAuth stays draft-only until
Graph send). Using `draft` on a K2-hosted message id errors with a
pointer to `k2 mail reply`. Graph compose-draft is out of v1.

USAGE
